module

public import WeilConjectures.SmoothPurity.PurityFiniteSetting.A1KummerEtaleData

/-! # The absolute finite-level Kummer calculation
Source: det-prop-a1-kummer.proof.md, Coefficients, Clause (c), Degrees 0 and 1.
-/

@[expose] public section
set_option autoImplicit false
universe u
open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits AlgebraicGeometry
namespace WeilConjectures.PurityFiniteSetting

/-- Absolute degree-one Kummer cohomology at every finite level.
Source: det-prop-a1-kummer.proof.md, Coefficients, Clause (c), Degrees 0 and 1
(blueprint: new-pur-a1-kummer-absolute-devissage).

Proof: first compute root coefficients. The Kummer exact sequence and H1(Gm)=Pic
identify H1 with units modulo m-th powers, since the polynomial and Laurent polynomial
rings have trivial Picard group. Their units are k* and k* times t^Z; divisibility of
k* makes the first quotient zero and the second Z/m generated by the boundary of t.
Primitive roots and connectedness identify H0 with the actual constant-section map;
this degree-zero computation is proved separately in a1KummerAbsoluteZero_isIso.
For level one choose a finite basis of the residue field over F_ell and apply the
finite biproduct identities to these cohomology computations. For successive levels
use the exact sequence A_(r-1) --pi--> A_r --> F. The maps and exactness are
Ideal.mulQuot, Ideal.quotOfMul and Ideal.exact_mulQuot_quotOfMul; the nonzero
uniformizer makes the first map injective, and the second is surjective. A common
primitive root trivializes all twisted coefficients and makes this a short exact sheaf sequence.
Constant H0
sections make H0(A_r) --> H0(F) surjective, so its connecting map is zero. The long
exact sequence transfers H1 vanishing on A1 and gives a short exact H1 sequence
on Gm: normalizedKummerGlobal_higher_isZero supplies the H2 vanishing at every
coefficient level from the affine-curve dimension bound.
The proved kummerCoefficientInsertion_cohomology_map shows that insertion maps commute
with both coefficient maps, including the module-linear pi inclusion. Compare this
sequence with the coefficient sequence; the short five lemma makes a |-> a*kappa(t) invertible.
Naturality of the root Kummer sequences
identifies the common-exponent boundary with the residue-exponent boundary. Induction
reaches P.level. Finally the normalized module/abelian class and global-sections
comparisons identify the resulting generator with a1KummerAbsoluteGenerator and
the line vanishing with H1 of a1KummerAbsoluteImage false.
This proves the statement without any free-module hypothesis at ramified levels. -/
theorem a1Kummer_absolute_devissage (P : PurityFiniteSetting.{u}) (_ζ : P.field.k)
    (_hζ : IsPrimitiveRoot _ζ P.diagonalExponent) :
    IsIso P.a1KummerAbsoluteGenerator ∧
    IsZero ((DerivedCategory.Plus.homologyFunctor _ 1).obj
      (P.a1KummerAbsoluteImage false)) := by sorry

end WeilConjectures.PurityFiniteSetting
